  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved decent employment opportunities through the development of employment programmes and policies in the Solomon Islands</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO has been supporting the development of Solomon Islands&apos; first-ever National Employment Policy (NEP)&#x2014; a coherent, comprehensive and integrated framework that promotes full and productive employment and decent work for all, in line with the SDGs. The NEP mainstreams employment in national policy-making and strives to achieve a dynamic and inclusive labour market by promoting job creation, enhancing skills development, and ensuring that employment opportunities are available and accessible to all.&#xa0;

The NEP draft has been finalized on the basis of an employment situation analysis as well as broad-based consultations and engagement with key stakeholders, including multiple government agencies, employers&apos; and workers&apos; organizations, and other relevant stakeholders. This collaborative and inclusive approach ensures that the NEP reflects stakeholders&apos; views, ensuring their support and commitment. By addressing several relevant areas, the ILO aims to create a dynamic and inclusive labour market that benefits everyone in the Solomon Islands. The Government plans to adopt the NEP in mid-2025 and then move forward with its implementation, following the action plan and implementation mechanisms that form part of the NEP. The work has been supported by the ILO-led joint programme &quot;Advancing the SDGs by improving livelihoods and resilience via economic diversification and digital transformation&quot;, funded by the Joint SDG Fund.</narrative>
  </description>
